Dear AIVOA Quality Assurance Team,

I am writing to formally report an adverse quality defect noticed at our Apollo Pharmacy Central Flagship branch in Bengaluru. 

During dispensing this morning, one of our senior pharmacists noticed abnormal color variation in your Amoxicillin capsules 500mg. Upon opening three unopened blister packaging strips from carton box lot number BMX24602, we observed that approximately 48 capsules exhibit severe brownish-grey spotty discoloration on the ivory-colored gelatin cap, whereas normally they should be uniform ivory and maroon.

The patients have been notified and we immediately stopped dispensing from this specific lot. In total, 48 capsules across 4 strips have been quarantined in our secure return lockbox pending your inspection and instructions. 

Could you please arrange for your medical sales representative to collect these affected samples for QC testing, or send us return documentation? Please confirm if there are any other reported incidents with batch BMX24602 and advise on appropriate CAPA containment actions.

Looking forward to your swift response.

